# Writing and UI Style

## No Emojis

Never use emojis in code, UI, comments, docs, or responses for this project.

Use icons instead:

- Use `feather-icons` via the shared `FeatherIcon` component (`src/components/ui/FeatherIcon.vue`)
- Store icon names as feather keys (e.g. `home`, `credit-card`), not unicode characters
- Navigation and categories: render with `<FeatherIcon name="home" :size="16" />`

```vue
<!-- Bad -->
<span>🏠 Housing</span>

<!-- Good -->
<HomeIcon class="w-4 h-4" />
<span>Housing</span>
```

## No Em Dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`, U+2014). Use commas, colons, parentheses, or separate sentences instead.

```markdown
<!-- Bad -->
BudgetRick is local-first — no bank connections required.

<!-- Good -->
BudgetRick is local-first with no bank connections required.
```

Hyphens (`-`) and en dashes (`–`) for ranges are fine when appropriate.
